WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Light a log in a fire and within

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.640
the hour it's ash, smoke and a warm

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.320
room.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.800
Now try the reverse.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.600
Put the ash, smoke and warm air together

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.840
and you will never get the log back.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.400
Yet a tree makes sugar and wood out

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.360
of carbon dioxide and water, all day long.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.680
So why does a fire run all the

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.920
way one way, while a tree can build

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:22.640
the other way?

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.200
To find out, we need two ideas from

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.560
Year 11: enthalpy, which is about heat, and

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.040
entropy, which is about spreading out.

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:34.986
Last time, a sealed flask settled into a

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.786
mixture where the forward and reverse rates matched

00:00:38.027 --> 00:00:39.786
and the amounts stopped changing.

00:00:40.427 --> 00:00:41.986
A fire is different.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.746
Its change keeps going one way until the

00:00:44.907 --> 00:00:47.546
fuel or the oxygen runs out, and nothing

00:00:47.627 --> 00:00:48.346
balances it.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.906
A system where the net change is still

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:53.786
going, with no steady balance, is called a

00:00:53.947 --> 00:00:55.546
non-equilibrium system.

00:00:56.187 --> 00:00:59.306
Combustion is one, and photosynthesis is another.

00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:02.826
They stay away from equilibrium for opposite reasons.

00:01:04.034 --> 00:01:05.233
First, heat.

00:01:05.874 --> 00:01:09.153
The enthalpy change, written delta H, is the

00:01:09.274 --> 00:01:12.193
heat a reaction gives out or takes in.

00:01:12.314 --> 00:01:14.913
A negative delta H means heat flows out

00:01:15.034 --> 00:01:17.473
into the surroundings, like a fire.

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:20.593
Giving out heat spreads energy into the surroundings,

00:01:20.714 --> 00:01:23.393
and that is why it helps a reaction.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.313
Second, spreading.

00:01:25.594 --> 00:01:28.753
Entropy, written S, measures how spread out the

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.233
particles and the energy are, in other words

00:01:31.474 --> 00:01:33.793
how many ways they can be arranged.

00:01:33.874 --> 00:01:36.753
The change in entropy is written delta S.

00:01:37.074 --> 00:01:40.033
A tightly packed crystal has low entropy.

00:01:40.074 --> 00:01:42.113
When it breaks into separate molecules that fly

00:01:42.194 --> 00:01:44.913
about, the particles are more spread out, so

00:01:44.994 --> 00:01:46.873
delta S is positive.

00:01:47.154 --> 00:01:49.713
Keep the two apart: heat leaving is the

00:01:49.794 --> 00:01:52.513
delta H term, and the particles spreading out

00:01:52.594 --> 00:01:55.233
in the reacting mixture is the entropy term.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.593
A reaction is helped along by giving out

00:01:58.754 --> 00:02:00.873
heat and by spreading out.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.233
You met the combination in Year 11, as

00:02:03.314 --> 00:02:06.033
one number called the free energy change, delta

00:02:06.194 --> 00:02:09.313
G, which equals delta H minus T delta

00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:12.433
S, where T is the temperature in kelvin,

00:02:12.474 --> 00:02:15.393
which is always positive, so T delta S

00:02:15.474 --> 00:02:17.913
has the same sign as delta S.

00:02:18.354 --> 00:02:20.833
If delta G is negative, the reaction can

00:02:20.914 --> 00:02:22.193
run on its own.

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.433
The word for that is spontaneous.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:29.393
Glucose plus oxygen makes carbon dioxide and water.

00:02:29.954 --> 00:02:32.273
Burning one mole of glucose gives a delta

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.833
H of minus two thousand eight hundred and

00:02:34.914 --> 00:02:38.033
three kilojoules, and at room temperature T delta

00:02:38.194 --> 00:02:40.793
S is plus seventy-eight kilojoules.

00:02:41.154 --> 00:02:42.193
First, heat.

00:02:42.674 --> 00:02:45.633
Delta H is negative, so heat flows out,

00:02:45.674 --> 00:02:46.673
and that helps.

00:02:46.994 --> 00:02:48.353
Second, spreading.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.793
A solid sugar crystal and six oxygen molecules

00:02:52.114 --> 00:02:55.473
become six carbon dioxide gas molecules and six

00:02:55.554 --> 00:02:56.913
liquid water molecules.

00:02:57.394 --> 00:03:00.113
The crystal is gone and seven particles become

00:03:00.194 --> 00:03:02.513
twelve, so there are more ways to arrange

00:03:02.594 --> 00:03:02.833
them.

00:03:03.314 --> 00:03:05.953
Entropy goes up, and T delta S is

00:03:06.114 --> 00:03:06.673
positive.

00:03:07.314 --> 00:03:10.513
Now, delta G is delta H minus T

00:03:10.674 --> 00:03:13.553
delta S, which is minus two thousand eight

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:16.993
hundred and three, minus seventy-eight, giving minus two

00:03:17.154 --> 00:03:20.513
thousand eight hundred and eighty-one kilojoules per mole.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:23.113
Both terms push the same way, but the

00:03:23.154 --> 00:03:25.633
heat term does almost all the work, and

00:03:25.714 --> 00:03:27.233
spreading adds a little more.

00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:30.313
How big is big?

00:03:30.594 --> 00:03:33.553
Minus two thousand eight hundred and eighty-one kilojoules

00:03:33.714 --> 00:03:36.273
is a very strong pull towards products.

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:39.193
The reverse reaction is so slight that the

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:42.193
leftover reactants can't even be measured, so we

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.353
treat the reaction as running to completion.

00:03:45.074 --> 00:03:47.233
As a rough guide, a delta G close

00:03:47.314 --> 00:03:50.193
to zero, within a few tens of kilojoules,

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.913
leaves a real mixture of reactants and products,

00:03:52.994 --> 00:03:54.353
like the flask last time.

00:03:54.914 --> 00:03:57.633
A delta G hundreds of kilojoules below zero

00:03:57.954 --> 00:03:59.873
leaves essentially all products.

00:04:00.354 --> 00:04:02.593
That is why ash never becomes a log

00:04:02.674 --> 00:04:03.233
again.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.913
While the fuel is still burning, the system

00:04:07.074 --> 00:04:08.913
is a non-equilibrium system.

00:04:09.474 --> 00:04:11.313
Once the fuel is gone and nothing is

00:04:11.394 --> 00:04:13.553
left to run, it is the static case

00:04:13.634 --> 00:04:16.673
from the first video: finished, with both rates

00:04:16.914 --> 00:04:17.753
zero.

00:04:18.194 --> 00:04:19.073
One warning, though.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.713
Delta G tells you where a change is

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.113
heading, not how fast it gets there.

00:04:24.674 --> 00:04:26.113
A bowl of sugar sits in the air

00:04:26.194 --> 00:04:28.353
for years, even though its delta G is

00:04:28.514 --> 00:04:31.873
hugely negative, until something gets it started.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.620
Now run it backwards.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.700
Photosynthesis makes sugar from carbon dioxide and water,

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.500
which is burning in reverse, so every sign

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:42.140
flips.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.020
Delta H is plus two thousand eight hundred

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.740
and three, because energy has to go in,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.380
and in a leaf that energy is light.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:53.340
Twelve particles become seven, and the sugar settles

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:56.300
into a crystal, so entropy falls and T

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.020
delta S is minus seventy-eight.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.900
Delta G equals delta H minus T delta

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.940
S: plus two thousand eight hundred and three,

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.100
minus negative seventy-eight.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.820
Minus a negative adds, so delta G is

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.860
plus two thousand eight hundred and eighty-one kilojoules

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:13.900
per mole.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.580
It can't run on its own at any

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.380
temperature.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.360
So how does a leaf do it?

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.760
A leaf is an open system.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.080
Sunlight keeps supplying energy, carbon dioxide keeps arriving

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:27.920
and oxygen leaves.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.360
Cut off the light and photosynthesis stops, because

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.360
nothing supplies the energy any more.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.920
The leaf's sugar can still be broken down

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.280
by respiration, but that is a separate process,

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.120
and it runs in the light and in

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:41.680
the dark.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.480
So it is the constant light input that

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:48.000
keeps photosynthesis going, away from equilibrium.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.080
Here's a way to hold onto this.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.840
When the two terms agree, heat out and

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.320
spread out, the reaction can run on its

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.000
own.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.760
Heat in and packed in, and it needs

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.920
energy fed in all the time.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:05.600
If the two disagree, work out delta G,

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.400
because the sizes and the temperature then matter.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.880
Your turn, with a new reaction.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.600
Hydrogen burns in oxygen to make liquid water:

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.080
two H two plus O two gives two

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.400
H two O.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.840
For the equation as written, which makes two

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.800
moles of water, delta H is minus five

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.080
hundred and seventy-two kilojoules, and T delta S

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.840
is minus ninety-eight kilojoules at room temperature, because

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.000
three gas molecules become a liquid.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.440
A sealed tube of hydrogen and oxygen sits

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.480
at room temperature and nothing happens for years.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.480
One: work out delta G.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.720
Two: if the gases did react, would you

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.400
end up with a mixture of reactants and

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.800
products, or nearly all products?

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:51.920
Give a reason.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.920
Three: why doesn't the unchanged tube contradict your

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:56.880
answer to two?

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.440
Pause the video if you'd like more time.

00:07:44.867 --> 00:07:47.826
Delta G is delta H minus T delta

00:07:47.987 --> 00:07:51.426
S, which is minus five hundred and seventy-two,

00:07:51.507 --> 00:07:55.026
minus the negative ninety-eight, so minus four hundred

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.706
and seventy-four kilojoules.

00:07:57.267 --> 00:08:00.306
The heat released outweighs the lost spreading, so

00:08:00.467 --> 00:08:03.066
delta G is still strongly negative and the

00:08:03.107 --> 00:08:04.946
reaction can run on its own.

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:07.826
Minus four hundred and seventy-four is hundreds of

00:08:07.867 --> 00:08:11.026
kilojoules below zero, so the reverse is negligible

00:08:11.187 --> 00:08:13.426
and the end would be nearly all water.

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:16.306
The tube doesn't contradict that, because delta G

00:08:16.387 --> 00:08:18.626
says where the change is heading, not how

00:08:18.787 --> 00:08:19.826
fast it gets there.

00:08:20.307 --> 00:08:22.546
If you got minus six hundred and seventy,

00:08:22.627 --> 00:08:25.746
check the sign: minus a negative adds.

00:08:26.227 --> 00:08:28.066
If you said a mixture because the entropy

00:08:28.147 --> 00:08:31.346
term opposes it, compare the sizes: the heat

00:08:31.427 --> 00:08:34.226
term is five hundred and seventy-two, the entropy

00:08:34.307 --> 00:08:37.266
term only ninety-eight, so heat wins by a

00:08:37.427 --> 00:08:38.266
long way.

00:08:38.547 --> 00:08:40.066
If you said the tube must be at

00:08:40.147 --> 00:08:44.146
equilibrium because nothing changes, remember what dynamic equilibrium

00:08:44.307 --> 00:08:48.066
needs: both reactions running at equal rates.

00:08:48.187 --> 00:08:50.546
This tube has not reacted at all, so

00:08:50.627 --> 00:08:51.426
it is neither.

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:54.553
So when a reaction runs one way to

00:08:54.594 --> 00:08:56.873
the end, or needs constant help to run

00:08:56.954 --> 00:08:59.553
at all, ask three questions.

00:08:59.834 --> 00:09:02.113
Is heat going out or in?

00:09:02.394 --> 00:09:04.713
Is it spreading out or packing in?

00:09:05.274 --> 00:09:07.553
Then combine them in delta G.

00:09:07.834 --> 00:09:10.233
A very positive delta G means it needs

00:09:10.314 --> 00:09:13.113
energy fed in all the time, like sunlight

00:09:13.154 --> 00:09:15.113
in a leaf, and that is why a

00:09:15.194 --> 00:09:17.673
tree needs sunlight while a fire does not.

00:09:18.234 --> 00:09:20.713
And delta G never tells you the speed.

00:09:21.354 --> 00:09:23.673
Next, we'll take a flask that is already

00:09:23.714 --> 00:09:25.673
at equilibrium and disturb it.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.340
Here are the key notes.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.500
Pause the video if you need more time

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:31.380
to copy them.
